w: My pra- yer hear, O God; give ear un- to my words at length.
w: Op- pres- sors seek my soul, and God set not be- fore their eyes.
w: He ta- keth part with ev’- ry one that doth my soul up- hold.
w: O for thy truth’s sake cut them off, and sweep them clean a- way.
w: Thy name, O Lord, be- cause ’tis good, with praise I will con- fess.
w: And his de- sire mine eye hath seen up- on mine e- ne- mies.
